arm: dts: rockchip: rock-pi-e: keep upstream vcc_host_5v for the OS

U-Boot's rk3328-rock-pi-e-base-u-boot.dtsi made vcc_host_5v switchable
(dropped regulator-always-on/boot-on) and set it as phy-supply of
u2phy_host. On the EFI boot path U-Boot passes this control DT to the
OS, and Debian's 7.3.4 kernel then hits timer/delayed-work memory
corruption and panics on most boots (ROCK Pi E v1.21, dotOS test plan
T3.1). Upstream Linux keeps the regulator always on with no phy-supply.

Drop the override so the DT handed to the OS matches upstream Linux.
Applies to U-Boot v2026.04 (88dc2788).

diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/rk3328-rock-pi-e-base-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/rk3328-rock-pi-e-base-u-boot.dtsi
index a30adb0b..53c8e999 100644
--- a/arch/arm/dts/rk3328-rock-pi-e-base-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/rk3328-rock-pi-e-base-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -34,15 +34,6 @@
 	};
 };
 
-&u2phy_host {
-	phy-supply = <&vcc_host_5v>;
-};
-
-&vcc_host_5v {
-	/delete-property/ regulator-always-on;
-	/delete-property/ regulator-boot-on;
-};
-
 &vcc_sd {
 	bootph-pre-ram;
 };
